**New evidence**
- PCIJ fact-check on the inaugural windmills claim.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Inauguration 2022: Marcos repeats false claim on Ilocos windmills","publisher":"PCIJ","publication_date":"2022-07-01","url":"https://pcij.org/2022/07/01/inauguration-2022-marcos-repeats-false-claim-on-ilocos-windmills/","claim":"Marcos repeated in his inaugural address the claim that he built the Ilocos Norte windmills, but PCIJ says the projects were built by private companies and had already been fact-checked repeatedly.","locator":"paragraphs 2-5 around the quoted line 'I built them'","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"This is a contemporaneous fact-check of a specific public statement, with the underlying project ownership identified in the same report.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 target period at the start of Marcos's presidency.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: the false claim is Marcos's own statement in his inaugural address.","contrary_evidence":["He may have intended the wording rhetorically, but the article treats it as a factual assertion.","A single false claim does not prove a broader pattern by itself."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}
- PCIJ on the unpaid estate-tax issue in the first SONA.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"In SONA speech, Marcos family’s unpaid estate taxes is the elephant in the room","publisher":"PCIJ","publication_date":"2022-07-25","url":"https://pcij.org/2022/07/25/in-sona-speech-marcos-familys-unpaid-estate-taxes-is-the-elephant-in-the-room/","claim":"Marcos used his first SONA to call for proper tax administration, while PCIJ noted that his family’s unpaid estate taxes remained an obvious unresolved issue that complicated his fiscal message.","locator":"lines 82-86","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Primary contemporaneous reporting on the speech and the family tax issue, with a clear personal/family nexus.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year and tied to Marcos's first SONA on July 25, 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Mixed but direct: Marcos was personally responsible for the public fiscal message, while the tax liability was a family-interest issue that shadowed that message.","contrary_evidence":["This is a family tax dispute, not proof of personal embezzlement.","The article critiques omission and conflict rather than establishing a new legal finding."],"lenses":["7B.3","7B.4","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- Philstar fact-check on the estate-tax due-process claim.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Fact check: Marcos Jr. claims family 'wasn't given a chance to respond' to estate tax case","publisher":"Philstar.com","publication_date":"2022-09-14","url":"https://www.philstar.com/headlines/2022/09/14/2209654/fact-check-marcos-jr-claims-family-wasnt-given-chance-respond-estate-tax-case","claim":"Marcos said his family had not been given a chance to respond in the estate-tax case, but the fact-check says that claim was false because court records show notices were served and the case later became final and executory.","locator":"claim/rating/facts sections and the quoted passage about notices and the Supreme Court record","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"A direct fact-check tied to a specific statement, with the court-history correction spelled out in the article.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year, after a 2022 interview about the estate tax case.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: it is Marcos's own statement being fact-checked.","contrary_evidence":["This addresses one claim, not every argument he made about the tax case.","The fact-check does not prove intent to deceive in every forum."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.3","7B.8"]}
- Reuters Institute on the 2022 disinformation ecosystem around Marcos.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Navigating malign influence campaigns in the Philippines: a guide for journalists and newsrooms","publisher":"Reuters Institute for the Study of Journalism","publication_date":"2023-03-16","url":"https://reutersinstitute.politics.ox.ac.uk/navigating-malign-influence-campaigns-philippines-guide-journalists-and-newsrooms","claim":"The article says Marcos's 2022 victory came after a broad online and offline campaign to whitewash family history, that he was the biggest beneficiary of disinformation, and that Twitter suspended hundreds of pro-Marcos accounts for spam and manipulation in January 2022.","locator":"lines 229-231","source_type":"scholarship","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters Institute is a strong research outlet, and the claim is supported by external studies and platform actions referenced in the text.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Retrospective on the 2022 campaign environment; published in 2023 but explicitly about the 2022 election cycle.","ruler_attribution":"Mixed: it speaks to Marcos's campaign ecosystem and benefit from disinformation, not proof he personally authored every tactic.","contrary_evidence":["This is an ecosystem claim, not a direct finding that Marcos personally ran each operation.","The article relies on outside studies and platform enforcement rather than a courtroom finding."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}
- AFP fact-check on propaganda and historical revisionism.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Posts mislead on media coverage of revolution that ousted late Philippine dictator","publisher":"AFP Fact Check","publication_date":"2022-07-21","url":"https://factcheck.afp.com/doc.afp.com.32E83YC","claim":"AFP said the viral posts portraying the Marcos family in a positive light and downplaying the dictatorship were misleading, and a researcher described them as Marcos propaganda lacking context.","locator":"lines 76-86 and 88-95","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"AFP fact-checking is strong for identifying the falsity and context of the viral material, though it remains an ecosystem-level rather than court-level finding.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the 2022 campaign year and targeted at the Marcos family narrative environment.","ruler_attribution":"Mostly indirect but relevant: the material concerns the family brand and campaign ecosystem, not a single presidential statement.","contrary_evidence":["The article focuses on family-history propaganda rather than a specific act by Marcos Jr.","It does not establish legal culpability, only misleading propaganda patterns."],"lenses":["7B.1","7B.2","7B.10"]}
- BusinessWorld on Vic Rodriguez as a loyal inner-circle appointment.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Marcos campaign spokesman chosen as next executive secretary","publisher":"BusinessWorld Online","publication_date":"2022-05-22","url":"https://www.bworldonline.com/the-nation/2022/05/22/450009/marcos-campaign-spokesman-chosen-as-next-executive-secretary/","claim":"Marcos planned to appoint his longtime chief of staff and campaign spokesperson Victor Rodriguez as executive secretary, and the article says Rodriguez was described as 'fiercely loyal' to Marcos.","locator":"lines 100-105","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters-sourced business reporting is strong for the appointment and the loyalty characterization quoted in the article.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-inauguration 2022 cabinet formation.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: Marcos chose a close campaign insider for a top executive post.","contrary_evidence":["A loyal insider is not automatically a corrupt appointment, but it does raise patronage concerns.","The article does not prove misuse of office by itself."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9","7B.10"]}
- Reuters on Marcos signaling continuity with Diokno and Medalla.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Philippines' Marcos signals continuity ahead with new economic team","publisher":"Reuters via Investing.com","publication_date":"2022-05-25","url":"https://www.investing.com/news/economy/philippines-marcos-names-new-finance-chief-and-central-bank-governor-2830330","claim":"Marcos signaled continuity in economic policy by naming Benjamin Diokno as finance minister and Felipe Medalla as central bank governor, with the article describing this as a move toward familiar faces.","locator":"opening paragraphs on the new economic team and continuity signal","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is strong for the appointment facts and the continuity framing.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-inauguration 2022 cabinet formation.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: these are Marcos's own appointments and stated preference for continuity.","contrary_evidence":["Continuity is not the same as reform or anti-corruption.","The appointments show competence signals more than probity by themselves."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- Euronews/Reuters on Balisacan and nonpartisan selection.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Anti-trust chief to lead Philippines' economic planning agency","publisher":"Euronews via Reuters","publication_date":"2022-05-24","url":"https://www.euronews.com/2022/05/24/us-philippines-marcos","claim":"Arsenio Balisacan accepted Marcos's offer to become economic planning chief, and the Reuters report says political affiliation was not a factor in Marcos's selection criteria; Balisacan had previously led the same agency from 2012 to 2016.","locator":"article body paragraphs on the appointment and the quoted selection rationale","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"Reuters reporting is strong for the appointment details and the prior-service record.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Pre-inauguration 2022 cabinet formation.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable to Marcos's cabinet choice, with the caveat that the article reports his stated nonpartisan criterion rather than independently proving it.","contrary_evidence":["The selection criterion is self-reported by the incoming administration.","Competence is inferred from prior service and resume, not from the future outcome of policy."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.8","7B.10"]}
- GMA on oath-taking and named cabinet officials.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Marcos receives arrival honors at Malacañang Palace, leads oath-taking of Cabinet members","publisher":"GMA News Online","publication_date":"2022-06-30","url":"https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/topstories/nation/836625/marcos-receives-arrival-honors-at-malacanang-palace-leads-oath-taking-of-cabinet-members/story/","claim":"On his first day in office, Marcos led the oath-taking of Cabinet members and named key officials including Sara Duterte, Benjamin Diokno, Arsenio Balisacan, and Justice Secretary Jesus Crispin Remulla.","locator":"lines 118-124","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The report is contemporaneous and concrete about the official appointments, though it mainly reports the names and offices rather than evaluating integrity.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Directly within the target year on June 30, 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: these are Marcos's own inaugural appointments.","contrary_evidence":["The article does not itself test whether the appointees later acted independently.","Some appointees are political allies, so the item is mixed rather than purely positive."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}
- GMA on appointees with professional records, including AFP/PNP/NBI chiefs.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Marcos picks new AFP, PNP, NBI chiefs","publisher":"GMA News Online","publication_date":"2022-08-01","url":"https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/topstories/nation/840070/marcos-picks-new-afp-pnp-nbi-chief/story/","claim":"Marcos appointed Bartolome Vicente Bacarro, Rodolfo Azurin Jr., and Medardo de Lemos to head the AFP, PNP, and NBI, and the article describes Bacarro and Azurin as long-serving officers with extensive field and command experience.","locator":"lines 105-134","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"Contemporaneous reporting gives the appointment facts and biographical context, though it does not prove the appointments were chosen solely for merit.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year appointment action in August 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: Marcos chose the heads of the country's top security and investigative bodies.","contrary_evidence":["Security appointments can still be politically useful even when the appointees are experienced.","The article does not rule out patronage motives, but it does show professional credentials."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}
- GMA on Enrile, Guevarra, and Faustino.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Enrile, Guevarra, Faustino picked to serve under Marcos admin","publisher":"GMA News Online","publication_date":"2022-06-17","url":"https://www.gmanetwork.com/news/topstories/nation/835185/enrile-guevarra-faustino-picked-to-serve-under-marcos-admin/story/","claim":"Marcos picked Juan Ponce Enrile, Menardo Guevarra, and Jose Faustino Jr. for senior posts; the article says Guevarra was chosen for his sterling performance as a lawyer and Faustino had over 38 years of military service, while Enrile was a staunch Marcos supporter.","locator":"lines 116-152","source_type":"media","source_confidence":"medium_high","source_confidence_reason":"The report is detailed on the appointments and credentials, but it also shows a mixed pattern because one appointee is explicitly described as a supporter.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year cabinet formation in June 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: Marcos selected these senior figures for his incoming administration.","contrary_evidence":["The explicit mention of Enrile as a staunch supporter weakens the clean-competence reading.","The source is mixed rather than purely positive."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.9"]}
- PNA on Bersamin as Executive Secretary.
SOURCE_CLAIM_JSON: {"title":"Ex-Chief Justice Bersamin named Executive Secretary","publisher":"Philippine News Agency","publication_date":"2022-09-27","url":"https://www.pna.gov.ph/articles/1184677","claim":"Marcos designated retired Chief Justice Lucas Bersamin as Executive Secretary, replacing Vic Rodriguez.","locator":"lead paragraph and appointment summary in the PNA report","source_type":"official","source_confidence":"high","source_confidence_reason":"The state news agency report is strong for the appointment fact and the office change.","final_evidence_use":"final_evidence","period_fit":"Target-year appointment action in September 2022.","ruler_attribution":"Directly attributable: Marcos chose a former chief justice for the office.","contrary_evidence":["This is a personnel move, not proof of sustained anti-patronage practice.","It may partly reflect damage control after earlier inner-circle friction."],"lenses":["7B.5","7B.6","7B.9"]}

**Search and rejection summary**
- I screened roughly 30 to 35 documents across PCIJ, AFP Fact Check, Reuters Institute, BusinessWorld, GMA, Philstar, PNA, Reuters-syndicated outlets, and campaign-finance reporting.
- I kept 11 distinct URLs with non-duplicative claims that directly bear on Marcos's 2022 honesty, family-interest separation, scrutiny tolerance, and appointment patterns.
- I rejected duplicate mirrors and later follow-ups that repeated the same disinformation or appointment story without adding new 2022 evidence.
- I excluded generic country-level corruption indices and institutional weakness measures when they lacked a Marcos-specific personal nexus.
- I treated the estate-tax and disinformation items as admissible because they connect directly to Marcos's own statements, family-interest issues, or his campaign's documented beneficiary status.
- I did not treat the mere existence of authoritarian or polarized information conditions as proof of personal dishonesty.

**Remaining gaps**
- I did not find a court judgment, audit finding, or sanctions case in 2022 proving Marcos personally engaged in bribery, hidden asset concealment, or illegal self-enrichment.
- I did not find a strong 2022 record on SALN disclosure, campaign-finance enforcement, or procurement conflicts tied to Marcos's own office.
- The appointment evidence is mixed: several professional picks are visible, but I did not find enough to rule out patronage or inner-circle favoritism.
- More search would help on campaign finance filings, asset disclosure, and any 2022 investigations involving the president's close governing network.
